<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Gmtrack</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>gmtrack &lt;player&gt; &lt;zone ...&gt; [hours]       (230)
gmtrack &lt;player&gt; any [hours]
gmtrack &lt;player&gt; off
gmtrack
</pre>
<p>Follows a player for a game master's event, so you needn't ask 
<a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Where</a> again and again. Every game master online hears, as 
"[gm Asta] 14:02 ...":
</p>
<ul><li>when the player enters or leaves one of the zones (with <b>any</b>,</li></ul>
<p>every change of zone; a room standing inside another counts as the 
outer room's zone),
</p>
<ul><li>when they die, or fall below a third of their hit points (once, until</li></ul>
<p>they're above half again),
</p>
<ul><li>when someone starts following them,</li>
<li>when they've been idle 10 minutes, and when they're back,</li>
<li>when they leave the game.</li></ul>
<p>A game master is a god with $gm in their info (set &lt;god&gt; add-info $gm). 
Nothing about the player changes. A move by magic (goto, teleport, 
recall, summon) is noticed at their next command, or within the minute.
</p><p>Tracking ends by itself after the hours you give (2 if you give none, 6 
at most), when the player leaves the game, or with <b>off</b>. Tracking a 
player again starts over. <b>gmtrack</b> alone lists who is tracked.
</p><p>Example:
</p>
<pre>gmtrack asta midgaard udgaard 3
</pre>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmlure</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmmem</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Where</a>
</pre>




</div>